Every clinician should discuss an opioid-driving-or-machinery-safety-effect with a patient.
If a clinician starts an opioid-therapy for a patient then the clinician should particularly discuss an opioid-driving-or-machinery-safety-effect with the patient.
If a clinician increases an opioid-dosage for a patient then the clinician should particularly discuss an opioid-driving-or-machinery-safety-effect with the patient.
If a patient uses a central-nervous-system-depressant with an opioid then every clinician should particularly discuss an opioid-driving-or-machinery-safety-effect with the patient.
Every opioid can possibly affect a safe-vehicle-or-machinery-operation-ability.
A central-nervous-system-depressant-example includes a benzodiazepine-example and includes an alcohol-example.
